# Date and time

## Single import point

Never import `dayjs` directly outside of `lib/date-time.ts`. Always use `@/lib/date-time`:

```ts
import { formatDate, formatDateTimeShort, endOfTodayIso } from "@/lib/date-time"
```

```ts
import dayjs from "dayjs"
```

The second form is forbidden.

## Storage vs display

- **Timestamps** are stored as UTC ISO 8601 strings (e.g. from Supabase `timestamptz`).
- **Display** always converts to `America/Sao_Paulo` at the last moment.
- **Date-only values** (`YYYY-MM-DD`) are civil dates — never apply timezone conversion to them.

## Formats

| Helper | Output / role |
|--------|----------------|
| `formatDate(value)` | `DD/MM/YYYY` — date portion of a timestamp |
| `formatDateTime(value)` | `DD/MM/YYYY - HH:mm:ss` — full timestamp |
| `formatDateTimeShort(value)` | `DD/MM/YYYY · HH:mm` — lists and history |
| `formatTime(value)` | `HH:mm:ss` |
| `formatDateOnly(value)` | `DD/MM/YYYY` — civil date, no timezone shift |
| `todayCivilDate()` | `YYYY-MM-DD` in `America/Sao_Paulo` |
| `endOfTodayIso()` | UTC ISO of end of today in `America/Sao_Paulo` |
| `datetimeLocalToIso(value)` | `datetime-local` / `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm` → UTC ISO |
| `getTimestampUrgency(value)` | `overdue` \| `soon` \| `later` |

## Invalid input

Helpers reject `null`, `undefined`, and invalid values. Guard nullable values at call sites before formatting (`createdAt ? formatDate(createdAt) : "—"`).

## Plugins active

`utc`, `timezone`, `customParseFormat`, locale `pt-br`.
